## Positive Validation

A controlled remote network connection was generated from WIN11-01 to WIN11-02.

The resulting network authentication remained visible after applying the tuned DET-006 logic.

```text
Positive Validation:
PASS
```

This demonstrated that the tuning did not eliminate the activity DET-006 was intended to detect.

---

## Negative Validation

Normal successful Windows authentication was compared against the tuned detection.

Authentication that did not meet the remote network criteria was excluded from DET-006.

```text
Negative Validation:
PASS
```

The tuning therefore improved specificity while retaining the intended detection capability.

---

## False-Positive Reduction

The primary source of noise was:

```text
All Event ID 4624 successful authentication events
```

The tuned detection reduced this population to:

```text
Event ID 4624
AND
Logon Type 3
AND
Non-local source address
```

This reduced unrelated successful-authentication activity presented to the analyst.

Exact baseline and tuned event counts were not retained in the sprint record and are therefore not represented here.

---

## Detection Naming Improvement

The investigation demonstrated an important detection-engineering principle:

> A detection should not claim more than its telemetry can prove.

Without supporting share-access telemetry, Event ID 4624 with Logon Type 3 establishes a remote network logon but does not independently establish administrative-share access.

DET-006 was therefore refined to accurately represent the observable behavior:

```text
DET-006 — Suspicious Remote Network Logon
```

